import{_ as i,o as t,c as a,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 953 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 19 | Eradicate Class Solidification","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 953 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 19 | Eradicate Class Solidification","no":953,"module":5,"tags":["Heavenly-Dao Rule","Rule 19","Class Solidification","Mobility","Myriad-Rank Republicanism"],"related":["36-Social Structure and Class Mobility","941-Equal Evolutionary Qualification","909-Contract Responsibility More-Work-More-Pay"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0953_模块5-规则十九-根除阶层固化.md","filePath":"en/0953_模块5-规则十九-根除阶层固化.md"}'),n={name:"en/0953_模块5-规则十九-根除阶层固化.md"};function s(r,e,l,u,c,h){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-953-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-19-eradicate-class-solidification" tabindex="-1">Entry 953 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 19 | Eradicate Class Solidification <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-953-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-19-eradicate-class-solidification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 953 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 19 | Eradicate Class Solidification&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Document 36 | Series: Complete Collection of Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-birth-determines-neither-the-terminus-nor-may-it-lock-the-starting-line" tabindex="-1">Introduction: birth determines neither the terminus, nor may it lock the starting line <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-birth-determines-neither-the-terminus-nor-may-it-lock-the-starting-line" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: birth determines neither the terminus, nor may it lock the starting line&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Rule 7 gave every being an equal admission ticket, but the old cosmos had a second lock — class solidification. Even if everyone may initiate, the strong&#39;s child is born in the sect&#39;s center, the weak&#39;s child at the mine&#39;s bottom; the former breaks through with casual cultivation, the latter exhausts himself only to touch Sense-Condensed Realm. Over generations, &quot;equal qualification&quot; is quietly hollowed out by &quot;unequal starting points.&quot; Heavenly-Dao Rule 19 must smash this invisible lock: birth, bloodline, family, and sect affiliation may not become an evolutionary ceiling; classes must be mobile, and must move.</p><p>The six top-level axioms here aim at social structure: the republican axiom of Myriad Races is this rule&#39;s direct source; the anti-predation axiom points out class solidification is predation&#39;s heritification of gains; the collective-ascension axiom requires society&#39;s upper and lower channels clear and whole-system lifting; the causal self-discipline axiom requires the mobility process not manufacture new unfairness; the law-first axiom lets &quot;solidification identification, mobility guarantee, anti-heredity&quot; be stipulated first by law.</p><p>It must further point out the newly added Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a floor basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. This axiom rewrites predation&#39;s meaning at the root: old-cosmos resources and Dao were finite, so predation involution was forced; in Heng Yuan Zhou everyone inherently possesses infinite origin, and predation loses meaning. What this Heavenly-Dao rule establishes is precisely the law guardrail of this new order of &quot;infinite origin, predation meaningless.&quot;</p><h2 id="i-rule-content-three-points-of-eradicating-solidification" tabindex="-1">I. Rule Content: Three Points of Eradicating Solidification <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-rule-content-three-points-of-eradicating-solidification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Rule Content: Three Points of Eradicating Solidification&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Anti-heredity</strong>: sect masters, law-anchor permissions, and high posts may not be hereditary, but all arise per the plane-sovereign strong-one four-dimensional assessment (Entry 911) and election;</li><li><strong>Guarantee mobility</strong>: under contracted-responsibility more-work-more-pay (Entry 909), juniors may continuously rise by contribution, and the strong&#39;s descendants have no &quot;inheritance priority&quot;;</li><li><strong>Subsidize starting points</strong>: for individuals from weak birth, via the Youth-Supreme path, D-route human-made Dao-rules soul rings, and the 20% activation strategy (Entry 910), make up the starting-point gap, rather than letting the Matthew effect run.</li></ol><p>Mobility is not &quot;must climb upward&quot;: the individual has the right to choose ordinary life; Heavenly-Dao rules only lock &quot;may not refuse to fall,&quot; and do not force &quot;must rise.&quot;</p><h2 id="ii-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">II. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Social-structure argument</strong>: the Social Structure and Class Mobility (Document 36) points out a healthy civilization&#39;s mobility is its vitality source; solidification is death;</li><li><strong>Anti-heredity argument</strong>: hereditarily passing the strong one&#39;s achievements to descendants equals privately sharing Myriad-Ranks&#39; co-created gains with one family, essentially predation&#39;s continuation;</li><li><strong>Efficiency argument</strong>: solidification locks massive geniuses at the bottom, wasting civilization&#39;s most precious evolutionary resource; eradicating solidification releases potential.</li></ul><h2 id="iii-execution-mechanism" tabindex="-1">III. Execution Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-execution-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Execution Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The Alaya Network monitors the &quot;mobility rate&quot; between strata; anomalously low mobility triggers a solidification warning;</li><li>All high posts are publicly competed-for, with assessment records network-wide traced, eliminating predetermined appointments;</li><li>Subsidized resources for weak-birth individuals are automatically delivered, no questions of birth, no favors owed;</li><li>A &quot;birth-discrimination review group&quot; is set up, specifically handling sects, units, and regions&#39; implicit exclusion of juniors.</li></ul><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Light</strong>: post competitions formalistic, predetermined-appointment tendency, rectify within a time limit;</li><li><strong>Medium</strong>: publicly pushing birth priority and bloodline hiring, relevant unit permissions frozen, enters conversion program;</li><li><strong>Heavy</strong>: rebuilding caste systems, writing class solidification into sect regulations, handled heavily under Rule 7 and Rule 10.</li></ul><h2 id="v-supervising-subjects" tabindex="-1">V. Supervising Subjects <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervising-subjects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervising Subjects&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s mobility-rate dashboard is the first layer; the Anchor Supervisory Committee checks competition fairness as the second layer; the Symbiotic Court adjudicates birth-discrimination cases as the third layer; each clan and the Youth-Supreme supervision corps exercise self-correction over their own solidification tendency as the fourth layer.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: geniuses locked at the bottom are the greatest waste; eradicating solidification releases them</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: predation-gain heritification is legislatively banned; under Axiom 6 everyone inherently possesses basic infinite power, and finite-resource predation loses meaning at the root</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type systems are &quot;destined by heaven,&quot; the protagonist&#39;s clan fated to tower over all beings; Heng Yuan Zhou high posts are publicly competed for, and no birth, however noble, is hereditary</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the five lineages, Youth Supremes, plant spirits, and planet-consciousness representatives all enjoy mobility channels</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: newly incorporated civilizations&#39; social structures automatically enter mobility-rate monitoring, preventing old solidification from being brought into Heng Yuan Zhou</li></ul><p>Eradicating class solidification must also face a reality: a completely equal starting point is neither possible nor necessary. What Heavenly-Dao Rule 19 pursues is not &quot;everyone identical,&quot; but &quot;starting-point differences compensable, terminus gates open.&quot; A Youth Supreme from a humble clan gains subsidy via the D-route human-made Dao-rules soul rings; a mediocre-talented one finds his own rhythm via contracted responsibility; the easygoing retain their floor per Axiom 6 and are not eliminated by the times. Solidification&#39;s opposite is not egalitarianism, but mobility — a humble youth may rise, and a wealthy youth may also fall; both upward and downward channels simultaneously clear, and that is eradicating solidification.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Eradicating class solidification lands &quot;equal qualification&quot; from paper to ground. Starting points may differ; the terminus must be open to all.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/36-社会结构与阶层流动.html">Entry 36 · Social Structure and Class Mobility</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/909_模块5-第八条-联产承包多劳多得.html">Entry 909 · Contract Responsibility More-Work-More-Pay</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/910_模块5-第九条-20％激活战略.html">Entry 910 · 20% Activation Strategy</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/941_模块5-规则七-一切生灵平等进化资格.html">Entry 941 · Rule 7 All Beings&#39; Equal Evolutionary Qualification</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',24)])])}const y=i(n,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,y as default};
